WEBVTT

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.790
Don't worry about it.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.630
The reinforcements are here.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.310
The Aquaria Project.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.080
In their plan to create an ideal world, 
the Fusion Dimension's Academia

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:39.380
has driven Heartland City, in the Xyz 
Dimension, to the brink of obliteration.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.980
A City Full of Smiles

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:23.190
Both the Tyler sisters and Supreme Commander 
Edo have been tragically defeated.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.810
That means I, Mamoru Noro, 
must make my well-timed debut,

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.430
and carry out the Professor's order 
that I destroy the Lancers!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.930
Prepare yourself, Yuya Sakaki...

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.240
When I order my entire army to attack,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.270
you'll be erased in an instant.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.400
Manoro doesn't seem to 
understand how duels work.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.910
The entire army can't fight at once.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.480
D-Don't mock me!

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.880
It was just a figure of speech.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.210
I just meant to rile them up.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.050
Go, Academia Army!

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.650
Edo?

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.220
Wh-What are you doing?

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.070
In this duel with Yuya, 
I have learned, beyond doubt,

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.980
that his father's way of thinking is correct!

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:07.690
Edo...

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.740
As Yusyo Sakaki said, duels exist 
to bring smiles to people.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.880
They are not tools of war!

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.580
Those of you who watched... 
I am certain you felt the same!

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.170
Yeah, I think so.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.280
Th-That's ridiculous!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.240
Open your eyes, Noro!

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.780
To terrorize the Xyz Dimension's 
peaceful people,

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.990
and steal their smiles... That is clearly wrong!

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:40.920
Are you, the supreme commander, 
criticizing the Aquaria Project?

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.770
That's equivalent to treason 
against the Professor!

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.350
I know that.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:50.010
But I shall walk the path I believe to be right.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:50.980
In order to so...

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.450
I shall happily bear the traitor's dishonor!

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.900
He's throwing off the mantle of command 
entrusted to him by the Professor?

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.220
Will he really turn against Academia?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.040
That's actually... kind of cool!

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.490
What are you talking about?

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.520
Don't tell me you're turning traitor 
and joining the Lancers, too?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.770
More like... joining Yuya?

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.610
D-Don't be ridiculous!

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:20.310
Come, Gloria, you were entranced by 
Yuya's entertainment duel, as well.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.010
G-Grace!

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.620
Be honest, Sis.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.560
We're joining them, too!

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.250
What?

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.790
Thanks, everyone.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.690
With your help, I'm sure we can bring 
smiles back to the Xyz Dimension!

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.530
Isn't that right, Ute?

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.000
Ute?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.230
Yeah...

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:48.970
Another version of me, from the Xyz 
Dimension, that lives inside me.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.520
He's saying...

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.840
To Heartland...

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.910
To my homeland... Please help 
us return the smiles.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.380
I shall.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.150
We shall return the smiles we stole 
from the Xyz Dimension's people.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.790
That is the work we shall spend 
the rest of our lives doing.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.410
Not possible!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.260
You'll all be purged, right here and now.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.990
The moment Edo declared his rebellion,

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:22.520
I officially ascended to the position of the 
Expeditionary Force commander.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.590
Now, go... Academia Army!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.710
Hey, did you forget someone?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.170
Th-That voice...

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.390
Kaito!

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.840
I'm the one on wanted posters 
all over Academia.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:37.380
You'll need to beat me first, right?

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.430
Though I don't think you can beat me...

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.620
Or rather, that you can beat us.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.940
Us?

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.080
That's...

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.530
The Resistance!

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:54.410
Kaito!

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.900
Are you the one who brought them?

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:57.720
That's right!

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:01.370
Kaito brought everyone together 
and said, "Let's save Yuya!"

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.470
Allen!

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.400
Don't worry about Syun!

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.510
Sayaka's looking after him at the base!

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:07.740
I see.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:08.980
Thank goodness.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:11.100
We of the Resistance

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.540
will put our lives on the line 
to protect our precious allies.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.620
If you're ready to do the 
same, then duel me!

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.020
N-No... I'd rather pass, I think...

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.560
I'm a bureaucrat, with no real 
battle experience, you see...

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.410
Everyone, listen to me!

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.570
We have been tasked with what 
is called the Aquaria Project,

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.380
but it is actually an invasion plan.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.850
This is against our ideals!

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.820
Thus, we must abandon this plan,

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.290
and work to restore the Xyz Dimension.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.550
This is not an order.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:56.490
I permit those who disagree 
to return to Academia.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:00.160
Those who wish to atone for the 
crimes we have committed,

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.470
please stay and help me.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.460
Edo...

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:21.650
They're late!

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.770
According to my calculations,

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:28.860
the soup should have been finished 
in 29 minutes, 58 seconds!

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.330
But the hands of the clock are already 
past the 30-minute mark.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.850
How long will they keep the citizens waiting?

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:36.730
We're here!

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:37.570
You're late!

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:39.920
Why do we have to do this?

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.720
Making people happy is the 
core of entertainment.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.280
This is training.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:47.750
Giving rations and medicine away for free...

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:52.010
Academia's army is also taking responsibility 
for rebuilding our homes.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.490
That's the least they can do!

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:58.880
And on top of that, they said they'd take 
Syun to headquarters to look after him.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.690
Are you all really okay with that?

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:04.460
That Edo guy is an enemy boss, isn't he?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:09.240
But they said their headquarters 
has the best medical facilities.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.440
I don't think Kurosaki will regain 
consciousness by lying here.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:17.960
He needs to see a proper 
doctor and get treatment.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:20.920
But I understand Allen's concerns.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:25.950
Even if Yuya's duel got through 
to him, it's still Academia.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.890
That isn't true. I...

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.450
I trust him.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.480
Kaito...

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:36.090
Dueling you and Syun opened my eyes, too.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:38.360
To the importance of allies...

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.860
The beauty of smiles...

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:43.400
That duels exist to protect those things.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:47.310
I'm sure he's also realized that.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.930
That's the reason he came here.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:54.410
To apologize for using duels to 
steal smiles from so many.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:59.220
If they've really recognized 
what they've done wrong,

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.810
then I must apologize, too.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:06.020
I also terrorized countless Academia soldiers.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.470
Kaito...

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:11.400
But that's because Academia 
turned your family into cards!

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.900
When Yuya was dueling Edo, he told me...

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.080
Was that Yuya?

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:19.700
No... Ute?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:20.740
Yes.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.170
Back then, Yuya said it.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:27.640
If we just keep getting back at the people 
who hurt us, we'll never end the war.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:32.420
That was the creed of Yuya's 
father, Yusyo Sakaki, too.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:34.390
Yusyo Sakaki?

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:40.140
That forgiveness is the only 
way to end a fight.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:43.180
Of course, some things cannot be forgiven.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.930
Closing your eyes to that can 
cause great pain to the heart.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.530
And yet, we're starting to open 
the way to the future

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:53.400
by having the courage to forgive.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.100
To create a peaceful future 
where anyone can smile.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:02.310
Kaito, you showed us that courage just now.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.840
Bearing the pain of losing your family,

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.560
but forgiving and apologizing for your part.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.470
Ute...

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.070
I agree with Ute.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:17.160
There is a way to restore those 
turned into cards to normal.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.500
Really?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:24.060
Turning people into cards is a way 
of collecting people's life energy.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.540
I'm told that once the new, 
ideal world is created,

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:29.460
the people will be revived there.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.830
You can restore them to normal?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.090
My family...

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.500
Is that true?

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.320
Yes.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.150
But then, where are the cards you gathered?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.840
They were sent to Academia.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:45.590
There's a transport device 
at our headquarters.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:51.730
People turned into cards are sent from 
here to the Fusion Dimension?

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:55.110
Yes, all of them were sent to Academia.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:59.170
My family is there?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.810
Go, Kaito!

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.050
Go and save them.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.800
Your family... And Ruri!

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:06.520
Ruri...

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:10.340
I'm sure Syun would say the same thing.

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:14.160
Yuya, you all go, too.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.850
Syun will be fine.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:20.030
Have faith in Edo and me to make 
Syun feel better, together!

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:23.450
Yes, I shall save Syun Kurosaki.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.160
Please trust me.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.010
You've said it so many times.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.900
But Ute and I do trust you.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:33.870
That's right... I'm grateful.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:37.030
But I need to apologize to you.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:42.150
I think I might have accidentally sent 
your father to another dimension.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:47.500
The man who taught me the 
true beauty of duels. I...

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.140
Dad's still alive.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.420
So I'm sure we'll meet again!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.860
I believe that.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.190
Yuya...

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:59.450
And... About what I asked you...

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.610
About the girl named Yuzu Hiiragi, yes?

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.860
I spoke to all of the soldiers, 
and none had seen her.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:11.720
I shall try to search for her myself.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:12.940
Thanks.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.380
Well, then, shall we?

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:16.700
Yeah.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.460
Yuya.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.220
Yeah!

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:20.950
Wait!

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:22.110
Allen?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.690
Here, these are for you.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:25.420
These are your...

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:26.860
A token of my thanks.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.160
Please accept them!

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:29.380
Allen...

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.040
What's this?

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.300
Little Fairy.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.660
Take her with you.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.540
I want to fight with you guys, too.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:49.510
Understood. With this card by 
my side, I will save Ruri.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:58.220
Kaito...

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.630
Let's go!

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:02.960
To the Fusion Dimension!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.530
Moving out.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:05.720
Yeah!

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:21.250
If we're going to fight Academia, 
now's our only chance!

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:27.520
Just now, a duelist called Joeri 
defeated five of our allies.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.360
At this rate, the entire You Show School

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:37.080
will be crushed before we 
can even fight Academia!

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.780
Right now, we have Hugo and Yuzu, 
from other dimensions, on our side.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:42.810
This is the time we should strike!

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:45.390
Rin and Serena are in Academia.

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:46.600
Ruri, too.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:50.780
To save them, we need to take this 
chance to breach Academia!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:52.580
I'll go, too!

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:54.950
Me, too!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.700
Understood.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.020
I'll go, then.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.280
No, sir...

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.640
Don't overtax yourself.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.990
Let us handle it.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.380
You students went to the trouble 
of escaping from Academia.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:13.320
I would never send you back!

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.990
I will go.

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:19.570
I will personally speak with Leo Akaba!

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.410
Sorry.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.780
But you won't be able to meet the Professor.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.980
You won't even reach Academia.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:29.160
Is that...

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.810
Dennis?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.350
That's right.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.420
It's been a while, Yuzu. 
You'll be coming with me.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:39.750
You're...

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.490
My, my... You're here, too?

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.520
Hugo, was it?

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:49.870
Your duel with Sawatari, in the Synchro 
Dimension, was extremely entertaining.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:55.110
Though as an entertainer, you still 
can't hold a candle to me.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:56.910
Give me a break!

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.610
Losing to Kurosaki stripped 
away your disguise.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.250
How dare you call yourself an entertainer?!

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.360
It wasn't stripped away...

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.920
I revealed it of my own free will.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.990
To make our duel more exciting.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.470
And as I'd hoped, we made 
the audience very happy.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:14.960
Dennis...

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.680
You know him?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:19.260
It's been a while, teacher.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:20.200
Teacher?

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.530
This takes me back...

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:27.860
Back in Heartland, I so admired 
the street duels you performed.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:31.860
Thanks to you, I awakened to the 
beauty of the entertainment duel.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:33.530
But...

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:38.180
I think my way of enchanting spectators 
is even better than yours.

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:40.150
Is that so?

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:42.300
Care to try me, then?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.530
I've brought quite an audience with me.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.090
How did they know...

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:51.390
We worked out where this place was

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:54.570
from the witness information 
we've been collecting.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:16:00.000
Sir, it must be destiny that you're 
in the Fusion Dimension, too.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:03.980
I'd like you to see how much 
your student has grown.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:08.180
Damn you... I won't sit here listening 
to your nonsense anymore!

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:08.880
Yeah!

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.410
We won't let our teacher fight.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:11.280
We'll fight you!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.150
Leave it to us!

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:14.940
Very well! I'll face you.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:17.340
Sir?!

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.590
Mr. Sakaki?

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.530
Stand back, all of you.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:28.570
I see you haven't matured 
at all since those days.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:29.690
What was that?

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:33.940
You've always been concerned 
only with external flashiness.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.750
But beneath the grandeur,

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:39.910
how much of a message can you 
communicate to people's hearts?

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:42.380
That's what's important!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:44.380
Enough of your boasts!

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:47.920
I prefer practical lessons to lectures.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.690
Let's get started, sir.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:51.450
Duel!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.460
First, let's see what you can do.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.710
I'll begin, then.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.350
I go first.

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:03.630
I set one card and end my turn.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.160
That's all?

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:06.870
Are you mocking me?!

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:08.620
Certainly not.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:12.350
I always try to get the most 
enjoyment out of everything.

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.560
This is the groundwork for that.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:17.210
I see. Then I won't hold back, either.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:18.870
My turn!

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:23.620
You said I haven't grown at all.

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:28.260
But since then, I've learned a lot 
of things, in a lot of places.

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:30.220
Allow me to prove it.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:33.500
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 3 
Performage Mirror Conductor

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:38.390
and Scale 6 Performage Fire Dancer!

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:43.570
This allows me to summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and 5 simultaneously!

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.680
Pendulum Summon!

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:48.070
Come out, my monsters!

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:52.150
First, Performage Ball Balancer!

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:56.170
Next, Performage Plushfire!

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:59.020
He went right to Pendulum?

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.440
It isn't over yet.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:02.790
Both of the monsters he 
summoned are Level 4.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:07.530
I overlay Level 4 Ball Balancer and Plushfire!

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.300
The show must go on!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:17.210
Sky magician, travel around 
the stage magnificently!

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:18.910
Xyz Summon!

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:24.180
Appear, Rank 4 Performage Trapeze Magician!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.920
But unfortunately, the show will end, 
just as it's getting started.

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:33.920
I use one Overlay Unit on Trapeze Magician

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.740
to activate its monster effect!

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:41.530
This allows Trapeze Magician 
to attack twice this turn.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.510
Trapeze Magician's attack points are 2500.

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:48.270
If you take two direct attacks,

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:51.000
your life points will be spent.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.640
Sad, isn't it?

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:57.290
Go! Battle, Trapeze Magician!

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.750
Attack Yusyo Sakaki directly!

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:17.430
I activate my trap Miraculous Hats!

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.290
He disappeared?

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:27.040
No need to fret! I'm right here!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.980
Inside those silk hats?

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.120
Indeed.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.520
Surely you agree that ending the big show

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.630
with one direct attack would be boring.

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:38.960
So I thought I'd prepare a little game.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.390
A game?

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:44.080
Inside one of these silk 
hats is a spell card.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:48.430
I am hiding in the other, with a 
monster with 0 attack points.

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:53.170
If you find the monster card and destroy 
it, battle damage is doubled.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:58.380
In other words, I'll take 5000 points 
of damage and lose.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:00.440
Too bad!

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:06.890
As I said before, Trapeze Magician's 
effect lets it attack twice.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:10.410
Which means I have a 100% 
chance of getting it right.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.090
Then, you leave me no choice!

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:15.880
Let us celebrate your victory 
with a big show.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.100
Now, which is your first choice?

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.160
I attack the right-side hat!

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:21.570
Go, Trapeze Magician!

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:27.240
You destroyed the spell 
card Wonder Balloons.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:31.290
Sorry. It isn't the monster, so battle 
damage is reduced to 0.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.230
But it ends now.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:36.910
Trapeze Magician attacks the left-side hat.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:40.020
Yes...

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.230
Paper Doll?

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:54.030
A spell card that can be used as a 
monster when it's in the hand?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:57.870
Which means... From the start, 
there was no right answer?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.970
Damn! While he was forcing 
me to play his game...

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.080
After them!

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:07.340
They said they're heading to Academia!

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:08.950
The harbor! Hurry to the harbor!

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:20.290
There they are!

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.260
Yuzu, don't leave my side.

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:35.510
Don't worry. I can protect myself.

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:44.370
I mean it... Stay with me!

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:47.190
I swear I'll keep you safe.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:49.600
Hugo?

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:50.920
Yuzu?

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:54.730
Yuzu!

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:56.680
Yuya...

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:02.020
I get to see Yuya again, too?

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.170
Now it's your turn.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:52.710
You're... Dennis?

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:55.070
Hey! It's been a while, Gonny.

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:59.260
Do you intend to kidnap Yuzu, like you 
kidnapped Kurosaki's sister, Ruri?

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:03.220
Answer him! And tell us 
where Serena is, too!

00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:07.080
Sorry, but I have business to attend to.

00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:09.230
Kachidoki, I'm leaving it to you.

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:14.010
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Shura's Bloodlust.

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:16.200
The fun is only getting started!
